"59_win_io_tests.mst — WinIoTests: the Windows twin of the POSIX file-I/O
 slice (WINARM sprint P5, sprint_p05_detail.md D5 row 2: 'TWIN as win_io
 over msvcrt's _open/_read/_write/_close'). Runs ONLY on Windows (guarded
 in 99_run_all.mst); loads everywhere — an FFI pragma resolves at call
 time, so on macOS these classes are inert definitions, exactly like the
 kqueue surface is on Windows.

 Scope, honestly drawn: this twins the FILE surface of PosixIoTests
 (create/write/read/seek/unlink + errno), which is what the CRT offers a
 clean fixed-arity path for. It does NOT twin the kqueue/readiness half —
 kqueue has no Windows equivalent at all; that is the IoWorker's own
 post-P5 slice (IOCP or WSAPoll — sprint_p05_detail.md's D5 Δ), not a
 file-I/O question.

 Every binding is fixed-arity. The UCRT spells POSIX names with a leading
 underscore (_open, _read, ...); the bindings below use the PLAIN names
 and the P5 resolver's underscore-alias probe finds the real export — the
 same posture P0 set when it renamed a Rust-side binding rather than
 gating the test. Notably _open's optional third argument is VARIADIC
 (like Darwin's open), so creation goes through _creat + _setmode, both
 fixed 2-arity — the same split world/61 uses (open-existing vs creat),
 for the same reason.

 GetLastError discipline (winkb's module doc, pinned in embed::tests):
 bind it as its own import, WARM the binding once (first-call RESOLUTION
 itself performs Win32 calls that reset the thread's last-error), then
 read it as the immediately-next FFI call after the failing one.

 Δ (P5, MEASURED here): a C-`int`-returning UCRT call's -1 arrives as
 4294967295 through `ret: #g`. AAPCS64 leaves x0's upper half UNSPECIFIED
 for a 32-bit return; the UCRT materialises results with w-register
 writes, which ZERO-extend — while Darwin's libc happens to sign-extend,
 which is the only reason world/61's `close(-1) = -1` assertion works on
 macOS. So every i32-returning Windows binding narrows guest-side
 (`WinIo i32:` below); only genuinely-64-bit returns (_lseeki64) read x0
 raw. Neither library is wrong — the width is simply not expressible in
 the g/f token vocabulary, and the binding author owns it."

"── WinIo: raw class-side CRT/kernel32 bindings, all fixed-arity ──────────"
Object subclass: WinIo [
    "kernel32: one committed page — the mmap analogue for GC-stable memory
     handed to native code. MEM_COMMIT|MEM_RESERVE = 12288 (0x3000),
     PAGE_READWRITE = 4 (the values world/tests/30's capstone proves)."
    WinIo class >> virtualAllocAddr: a size: s type: t protect: p [
        <primitive: FFI function: #VirtualAlloc ret: #g args: #(g g g g)>
    ]
    WinIo class >> allocPage [ ^self virtualAllocAddr: 0 size: 4096 type: 12288 protect: 4 ]

    "UCRT file I/O (resolver finds _open, _creat, ... via the underscore
     alias). open is the 2-arg no-mode form: NEVER pass O_CREAT through it
     — the third (mode) argument is variadic; create with creat: instead."
    WinIo class >> openPath: p flags: f [
        <primitive: FFI function: #open ret: #g args: #(g g)>
    ]
    WinIo class >> creatPath: p mode: m [
        <primitive: FFI function: #creat ret: #g args: #(g g)>
    ]
    "_setmode(fd, _O_BINARY=32768): byte-exact I/O — the CRT defaults to
     text mode, which rewrites 0x0A on the way through."
    WinIo class >> setmodeFd: fd mode: m [
        <primitive: FFI function: #setmode ret: #g args: #(g g)>
    ]
    WinIo class >> read: fd into: b count: n [
        <primitive: FFI function: #read ret: #g args: #(g g g)>
    ]
    WinIo class >> write: fd from: b count: n [
        <primitive: FFI function: #write ret: #g args: #(g g g)>
    ]
    WinIo class >> close: fd [
        <primitive: FFI function: #close ret: #g args: #(g)>
    ]
    "_lseeki64 — the 64-bit-offset seek (plain _lseek returns a 32-bit
     long on Windows)."
    WinIo class >> lseekFd: fd offset: o whence: w [
        <primitive: FFI function: #lseeki64 ret: #g args: #(g g g)>
    ]
    WinIo class >> unlinkPath: p [
        <primitive: FFI function: #unlink ret: #g args: #(g)>
    ]
    "errno lives behind _errno() — a 0-arg function answering int*, the
     exact shape of Darwin's __error() that Posix errno composes."
    WinIo class >> errnoAddress [
        <primitive: FFI function: #errno ret: #g args: #()>
    ]
    WinIo class >> errno [
        | a |
        a := Alien forAddress: self errnoAddress size: 4.
        ^(a byteAt: 1) + ((a byteAt: 2) * 256)
            + ((a byteAt: 3) * 65536) + ((a byteAt: 4) * 16777216)
    ]

    "kernel32: temp directory (so the round-trip file never lands in the
     repo checkout), plus the GetLastError pair for the discipline test."
    WinIo class >> tempPathMax: n into: buf [
        <primitive: FFI function: #GetTempPathA ret: #g args: #(g g)>
    ]
    WinIo class >> closeHandle: h [
        <primitive: FFI function: #CloseHandle ret: #g args: #(g)>
    ]
    WinIo class >> getLastError [
        <primitive: FFI function: #GetLastError ret: #g args: #()>
    ]

    "── constants: UCRT values, NOT Darwin's (O_CREAT is 256 here, 512
     there; O_BINARY has no Darwin counterpart at all) ──"
    WinIo class >> oRdOnly [ ^0 ]
    WinIo class >> oWrOnly [ ^1 ]
    WinIo class >> oBinary [ ^32768 ]
    WinIo class >> seekSet [ ^0 ]
    WinIo class >> seekEnd [ ^2 ]
    WinIo class >> defaultMode [ ^384 ]     "_S_IREAD|_S_IWRITE = 0x180"

    "Narrow a C-`int` return read raw from x0 (this file's header Δ: the
     UCRT zero-extends via w-register writes, so -1 reads as 4294967295)."
    WinIo class >> i32: v [
        ^v >= 2147483648 ifTrue: [ v - 4294967296 ] ifFalse: [ v ]
    ]
]

"── NativeBuffer reopened: a VirtualAlloc-backed page ─────────────────────
 NativeBuffer's own initPage rides Posix mmapPage, which cannot resolve on
 Windows; winPage is the twin constructor over kernel32, reusing every
 accessor (byteAt:, u16At:, u32At:, i64At:, zero:at:) unchanged — the
 reopen-after-defining pattern world/61 itself uses for Posix."
Object subclass: NativeBuffer [
    NativeBuffer class >> winPage [ ^self basicNew initWinPage ]
    initWinPage [
        addr := WinIo allocPage.
        alien := Alien forAddress: addr size: 4096.
        ^self
    ]
]

TestCase subclass: WinIoTests [
    WinIoTests class >> isEnabled ^ <Boolean> [
        "WG9-2: the gate that used to live only in
         `99_run_all.mst`'s guards, moved here so DISCOVERY can see
         it too (`TestRunner allTestClasses`). platform-gated; see 99_run_all.mst's bookkeeping note."
        ^Smalltalk platformName == #windows
    ]

    runAll [
        self runTest: #testCreateWriteReadRoundTrip do: [ self testCreateWriteReadRoundTrip ].
        self runTest: #testLseekEndReportsSize do: [ self testLseekEndReportsSize ].
        self runTest: #testOpenMissingFileFailsWithErrno do: [ self testOpenMissingFileFailsWithErrno ].
        self runTest: #testUnlinkRemoves do: [ self testUnlinkRemoves ].
        self runTest: #testGetLastErrorDiscipline do: [ self testGetLastErrorDiscipline ].
    ]

    "Stage the temp-dir path + `name` as a NUL-terminated C string at the
     buffer head; answer the staged path's address. GetTempPathA answers
     the copied LENGTH (trailing backslash included) and needs no
     GetLastError on this success path."
    stagePath: name in: buf [
        | len |
        len := WinIo tempPathMax: 300 into: buf address.
        self assert: len > 0.
        self assert: len < 300.
        1 to: name size do: [ :i |
            buf byteAt: len + i - 1 put: (name basicByteAt: i) ].
        buf byteAt: len + name size put: 0.
        ^buf address
    ]

    "create -> write 5 bytes (0x0A included: binary mode must not rewrite
     it) -> close -> open -> read back -> byte-exact compare."
    testCreateWriteReadRoundTrip [
        | buf path fd wrote got |
        buf := NativeBuffer winPage.
        path := self stagePath: 'macvm_p5_winio.tmp' in: buf.
        fd := WinIo i32: (WinIo creatPath: path mode: WinIo defaultMode).
        self assert: fd >= 0.
        WinIo setmodeFd: fd mode: WinIo oBinary.
        buf byteAt: 512 put: 87.    "W"
        buf byteAt: 513 put: 73.    "I"
        buf byteAt: 514 put: 78.    "N"
        buf byteAt: 515 put: 10.    "LF — the byte text mode would rewrite"
        buf byteAt: 516 put: 90.    "Z"
        wrote := WinIo write: fd from: buf address + 512 count: 5.
        self assert: wrote = 5.
        self assert: (WinIo close: fd) = 0.

        fd := WinIo i32: (WinIo openPath: path flags: WinIo oRdOnly).
        self assert: fd >= 0.
        WinIo setmodeFd: fd mode: WinIo oBinary.
        got := WinIo read: fd into: buf address + 600 count: 5.
        self assert: got = 5.
        self assert: (buf byteAt: 600) = 87.
        self assert: (buf byteAt: 601) = 73.
        self assert: (buf byteAt: 602) = 78.
        self assert: (buf byteAt: 603) = 10.
        self assert: (buf byteAt: 604) = 90.
        WinIo close: fd.
        WinIo unlinkPath: (self stagePath: 'macvm_p5_winio.tmp' in: buf).
    ]

    testLseekEndReportsSize [
        | buf path fd |
        buf := NativeBuffer winPage.
        path := self stagePath: 'macvm_p5_winio2.tmp' in: buf.
        fd := WinIo i32: (WinIo creatPath: path mode: WinIo defaultMode).
        self assert: fd >= 0.
        WinIo setmodeFd: fd mode: WinIo oBinary.
        buf byteAt: 512 put: 65. buf byteAt: 513 put: 66. buf byteAt: 514 put: 67.
        self assert: (WinIo write: fd from: buf address + 512 count: 3) = 3.
        self assert: (WinIo lseekFd: fd offset: 0 whence: WinIo seekEnd) = 3.
        "seek back and re-read one byte to prove the cursor really moved"
        self assert: (WinIo lseekFd: fd offset: 1 whence: WinIo seekSet) = 1.
        self assert: (WinIo read: fd into: buf address + 700 count: 1) = 1.
        self assert: (buf byteAt: 700) = 66.
        WinIo close: fd.
        WinIo unlinkPath: (self stagePath: 'macvm_p5_winio2.tmp' in: buf).
    ]

    "A missing file answers -1 and errno = ENOENT (2) — negative returns
     and the errno channel both cross the FFI, the twin of PosixIoTests'
     testNegativeReturnComesThrough/testErrnoReadable pair. (close(-1) is
     deliberately NOT the probe here: the UCRT routes an invalid fd
     through its parameter-validation machinery, which is a different
     contract than Darwin's EBADF return.)"
    testOpenMissingFileFailsWithErrno [
        | buf path fd |
        buf := NativeBuffer winPage.
        path := self stagePath: 'macvm_p5_winio_no_such_file.tmp' in: buf.
        WinIo unlinkPath: path.
        fd := WinIo i32: (WinIo openPath: path flags: WinIo oRdOnly).
        self assert: fd = -1.
        self assert: WinIo errno = 2.
    ]

    testUnlinkRemoves [
        | buf path fd |
        buf := NativeBuffer winPage.
        path := self stagePath: 'macvm_p5_winio3.tmp' in: buf.
        fd := WinIo i32: (WinIo creatPath: path mode: WinIo defaultMode).
        self assert: fd >= 0.
        WinIo close: fd.
        self assert: (WinIo unlinkPath: path) = 0.
        self assert: (WinIo i32: (WinIo openPath: path flags: WinIo oRdOnly)) = -1.
    ]

    "The v1 GetLastError discipline end to end from guest code: warm both
     bindings (first-call resolution performs Win32 calls that reset the
     per-thread error), fail CloseHandle(NULL), read 6 =
     ERROR_INVALID_HANDLE as the immediately-next FFI call."
    testGetLastErrorDiscipline [
        WinIo getLastError.
        self assert: (WinIo closeHandle: 0) = 0.
        self assert: WinIo getLastError = 6.
    ]
]
